INT. NIGHT BUS - MOVING - NIGHT

WE SEE a half-empty bus crossing the city in heavy rain.

Rain.

CLOSE ON TESS, 17, forehead against the cold window. She is angry, and she is trying to hide that she is angry, which is very obvious to the audience.

Her phone. Dead.

Dark streets. Nothing.

A woman's phone RINGS from Tess's bag. Not Tess's phone. Her mother's old phone, which she took without asking.

INSERT - PHONE SCREEN: "MUM CALLING".

Tess looks at it. Does not answer. It rings again.

Silence.

She answers.

LORNA (V.O.)
Tess? Where are you? It's one in the morning!

TESS
On a bus.

LORNA (V.O.)
Which bus? Which road? I have been calling for hours.

TESS
You were calling the other phone. The dead one.

ANGLE ON Tess's hand, gripping the phone so hard her knuckles go white. This is the last time they will speak before everything changes.

LORNA (V.O.)
Come home. We can talk about Dad in the morning.

TESS
There is nothing to talk about. You didn't tell me, Mum. He's been gone for a month and you let me think he was on a trip.

Nothing.

LORNA (V.O.)
I was trying to protect you.

TESS
(screaming now)
You were protecting YOURSELF!

The other passengers turn. The driver's eyes in the mirror.

BACK TO SCENE. Tess stands, the phone raised like she will throw it.

TESS (CONT'D)
Don't call me again!

She throws it. It SMASHES against the bus floor.

Rain. Only rain.
